  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In the circuit shown below, maximum Zener diode current will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>mA</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0072_f8c9e0f49bf4.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 126px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "9",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><meta charset=\"utf-8\" /><meta charset=\"utf-8\" /><img src=\"assets\\st0072_893fa55730c5.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 143px;\" /><b>​​​​​​​</b></p><p>Current through load resistor is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>10000</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&Omega;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>006</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&nbsp;and current through&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4000</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&Omega;</mi></math>&nbsp;resistor is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>120</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>60</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4000</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&Omega;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>015</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p><p>Thus, maximum current through Zener diode is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>015</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>006</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>009</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>mA</mi></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
